{
  "_comment": [
    "Shared conformance scenarios. One definition, three implementations.",
    "",
    "Each scenario names a sequence of SDK calls, the responses the mock server should return, and",
    "the wire trace plus decoded values every language must produce. The driver for each language",
    "makes the calls natively \u2014 `client.orgs.listMembers(...)` in TypeScript, `client.orgs.list_members(...)`",
    "in Python, `client.Orgs.ListMembers(...)` in Go \u2014 and reports what it observed.",
    "",
    "The runner then asserts two things: that each driver matches `expect`, and that all drivers agree",
    "with each other. The second is the one that actually proves the product's central claim, because",
    "a shared bug in the expectations would pass the first check and fail the second."
  ],
  "scenarios": [
    {
      "name": "list_categories",
      "why": "Decoding an array of objects at the response root, with a nested recursive field.",
      "responses": [
        {
          "status": 200,
          "json": [
            {
              "slug": "tools",
              "name": "Tools"
            },
            {
              "slug": "parts",
              "name": "Parts"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "expect": {
        "requests": [
          {
            "method": "GET",
            "path": "/categories",
            "query": {}
          }
        ],
        "values": {
          "count": 2,
          "first_slug": "tools",
          "second_name": "Parts"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "paginate_members",
      "why": "Cursor pagination through an envelope. The second request must carry the cursor, or the iterator refetches page one forever \u2014 a bug the TypeScript runtime actually shipped.",
      "responses": [
        {
          "status": 200,
          "json": {
            "data": [
              {
                "id": "11111111-1111-4111-8111-111111111111",
                "email": "a@example.com",
                "role": "admin"
              }
            ],
            "next_cursor": "c2",
            "total": 3
          }
        },
        {
          "status": 200,
          "json": {
            "data": [
              {
                "id": "22222222-2222-4222-8222-222222222222",
                "email": "b@example.com",
                "role": "member"
              }
            ],
            "next_cursor": "c3",
            "total": 3
          }
        },
        {
          "status": 200,
          "json": {
            "data": [
              {
                "id": "33333333-3333-4333-8333-333333333333",
                "email": "c@example.com",
                "role": "viewer"
              }
            ],
            "next_cursor": "",
            "total": 3
          }
        }
      ],
      "expect": {
        "requests": [
          {
            "method": "GET",
            "path": "/orgs/o1/members",
            "query": {
              "limit": "2"
            }
          },
          {
            "method": "GET",
            "path": "/orgs/o1/members",
            "query": {
              "limit": "2",
              "cursor": "c2"
            }
          },
          {
            "method": "GET",
            "path": "/orgs/o1/members",
            "query": {
              "limit": "2",
              "cursor": "c3"
            }
          }
        ],
        "values": {
          "emails": "a@example.com,b@example.com,c@example.com",
          "count": 3
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "query_serialization",
      "why": "Every language must put the same bytes on the wire. An omitted optional parameter is absent, not empty.",
      "responses": [
        {
          "status": 200,
          "json": [
            {
              "id": "11111111-1111-4111-8111-111111111111",
              "email": "a@example.com",
              "role": "admin"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "expect": {
        "requests": [
          {
            "method": "GET",
            "path": "/search",
            "query": {
              "q": "sprocket",
              "kind": "member"
            }
          }
        ],
        "values": {
          "count": "1"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "path_escaping",
      "why": "A path parameter containing a slash must be escaped, or the request addresses a different endpoint. A correctness issue, arguably a security one.",
      "responses": [
        {
          "status": 200,
          "body": "%PDF-1.4 fake",
          "contentType": "application/pdf"
        }
      ],
      "expect": {
        "requests": [
          {
            "method": "GET",
            "path": "/orgs/a%2Fb/invoices/i1/pdf",
            "query": {}
          }
        ],
        "values": {
          "byte_length": "13"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "error_404",
      "why": "A 404 must arrive as a narrowable typed error carrying the status, the server's message, and the request id.",
      "responses": [
        {
          "status": 404,
          "json": {
            "message": "Organisation not found"
          },
          "headers": {
            "x-request-id": "req_abc123"
          }
        }
      ],
      "expect": {
        "requests": [
          {
            "method": "GET",
            "path": "/orgs/missing/members",
            "query": {}
          }
        ],
        "values": {
          "error_kind": "not_found",
          "status": "404",
          "message": "Organisation not found",
          "request_id": "req_abc123"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "retry_then_success",
      "why": "A 503 on a POST is retried only when an idempotency key is present, and the retry must resend an identical request. Without a key it is not retried at all: deduplication has to happen on the server, and an io.Reader body read once would send nothing the second time.",
      "responses": [
        {
          "status": 503,
          "json": {
            "message": "try later"
          }
        },
        {
          "status": 200,
          "json": {
            "accepted": true,
            "event_id": "e1"
          }
        }
      ],
      "expect": {
        "requests": [
          {
            "method": "POST",
            "path": "/events",
            "query": {},
            "bodyKeys": "type"
          },
          {
            "method": "POST",
            "path": "/events",
            "query": {},
            "bodyKeys": "type"
          }
        ],
        "values": {
          "accepted": "true",
          "event_id": "e1"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "no_retry_on_400",
      "why": "A 400 was understood and rejected. Resending it is pure load on someone else's service, even with an idempotency key.",
      "responses": [
        {
          "status": 400,
          "json": {
            "message": "bad request"
          }
        }
      ],
      "expect": {
        "requests": [
          {
            "method": "POST",
            "path": "/events",
            "query": {},
            "bodyKeys": "type"
          }
        ],
        "values": {
          "error_kind": "bad_request"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "text_response",
      "why": "A CSV export is text, not opaque bytes. Typing it as a blob forces callers to unwrap something that was always a string.",
      "responses": [
        {
          "status": 200,
          "body": "month,total\n2026-01,42\n",
          "contentType": "text/csv"
        }
      ],
      "expect": {
        "requests": [
          {
            "method": "GET",
            "path": "/reports/usage",
            "query": {}
          }
        ],
        "values": {
          "text_starts_with": "month,total",
          "line_count": "2"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "validation_catches_a_broken_contract",
      "why": "Every language must reject a response missing a required field, and name the same path. This is what makes the validation guarantee identical rather than merely present in three places.",
      "responses": [
        {
          "status": 200,
          "json": [
            {
              "slug": "tools"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "expect": {
        "requests": [
          {
            "method": "GET",
            "path": "/categories",
            "query": {}
          }
        ],
        "values": {
          "error_kind": "validation",
          "path": "[0].name"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "validation_allows_an_additive_field",
      "why": "An API that grew must never break a client. All three languages must accept an unknown field at every level.",
      "responses": [
        {
          "status": 200,
          "json": [
            {
              "slug": "tools",
              "name": "Tools",
              "added_next_quarter": {
                "nested": true
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "expect": {
        "requests": [
          {
            "method": "GET",
            "path": "/categories",
            "query": {}
          }
        ],
        "values": {
          "count": "1",
          "first_slug": "tools"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "validation_on_a_paginated_response",
      "why": "Paginated methods call the transport directly, so they bypassed validation entirely \u2014 every list response went unchecked from the moment validation shipped. A list method is the most common thing in an SDK, so this was most of the surface.",
      "responses": [
        {
          "status": 200,
          "json": {
            "data": [
              {
                "id": "11111111-1111-4111-8111-111111111111",
                "role": "admin"
              }
            ],
            "next_cursor": "",
            "total": 1
          }
        }
      ],
      "expect": {
        "requests": [
          {
            "method": "GET",
            "path": "/orgs/o1/members",
            "query": {}
          }
        ],
        "values": {
          "error_kind": "validation",
          "path": "email"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "no_retry_without_idempotency_key",
      "why": "A POST returning 503 must NOT be retried without an idempotency key. This was a real bug \u2014 a `POST /charges` was sent three times, and whether the server processed the first is unknowable from the client.",
      "responses": [
        {
          "status": 503,
          "json": {
            "message": "try later"
          }
        }
      ],
      "expect": {
        "requests": [
          {
            "method": "POST",
            "path": "/events",
            "query": {},
            "bodyKeys": "type"
          }
        ],
        "values": {
          "error_kind": "server_error"
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
